WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.370
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.170
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Ingram Activated!

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.120
What is this
world coming to?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.880
Here he comes!

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:27.140
Bulldog pilot: Halt your
Labor and exit the cockpit!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.850
Come on, Shinohara!
We've got him on a DWI.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.560
I'll yank him out of that
cockpit and finish this.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.310
Wait.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.110
Shut up! What's the
matter with drinking?

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.530
You can't
drink and drive.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.370
We don't have time
for polite chitchat!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.870
You don't know what
I have to put up with!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.870
Come down and
we'll talk about it.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.630
You don't
know anything!

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.750
That does it!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.920
Wait, Ota!

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.800
I'll let my Labor
do the talking!

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.640
Surrender!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.060
Let me go!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.270
You coward!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.860
Let go!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.070
Idiot.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:30.080
Fight like a man! Aren't
you ashamed of yourself?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.040
I know I'm ashamed.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.710
Ota, look out
behind you!

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.160
How's Ota?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.040
He'll live.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.890
I'm amazed that
this thing is still in one piece.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.730
How's it look, Shige?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.810
Pretty hopeless. We can't
even salvage it for parts.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.110
Mr. Sakaki, this is our
chance to upgrade!

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.410
A new Labor won't help unless
we upgrade drivers, too.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.160
What?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.820
You have too much energy.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.330
It's one of my best points, Sir!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.370
Then you and your
teammates can go jogging.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.300
They're looking pretty good.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.430
Where were you, Captain Goto?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.970
Headquarters.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.600
About the new Labor model?

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.680
I finished the paperwork.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.560
You got it, even after
today's disaster?

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.650
It was perfect timing.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:27.400
It proved that we can't keep
using Division 1 's leftovers.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.490
But...

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:33.530
The competition in the Labor
market leads to rapid progress.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.580
They've modified your model 97.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:43.500
It looks like an instant classic.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:50.090
Is your problem a shortage of
Labors, or of talented officers?

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:57.770
Good point. But they're holding
aptitude tests in Hachioji today.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.730
Who knows? Maybe Division 2
will turn into an elite unit.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:08.400
Or maybe we'll become a gang
of thugs. I can't wait to find out.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.780
Spot any promising
candidates?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.040
This is my stop!

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.840
I'm late!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.340
This is the
spot, isn't it?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.780
The famous
first-generation Patlabor!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.830
Oh, no! I'm late!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.290
Who's that?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.840
You got a little carried
away this morning.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.470
Yeah, and he didn't
even land a punch.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.140
Can you fix it?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:23.140
Of course! But why bother?
We don't need this Labor.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.270
Didn't the
Captain tell you?

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.520
Then...?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.690
Want to see it?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.330
Finally! The new model
I've been longing for!

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:11.110
You're with Special
Vehicles, aren't you?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:12.440
Uh, yeah...

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.950
I've wanted to be like you
ever since I was a child!

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.320
You mean, pilot Labors?

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:27.580
I'm here for the Labor aptitude
test, but I seem to be lost.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.880
A Labor officer?
YOU?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.880
The aptitude test is
in the East Building.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.390
Where's that?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.260
Back the way
you came from.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.180
You mean I came
the wrong way?

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:45.850
Roger!

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.600
Excuse me!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:52.980
Strange kid.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:03.490
Here it is! Shinohara Heavy
Industries' finest product...

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:09.710
our new Police Labor!
Model 98-AV, aka: the Ingram!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.170
Can we see it?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.550
Let me take the cover off.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.300
What's going on?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.180
Who authorized this?

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.680
Mr. Jitsuyama,
look out!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:41.070
Close the main gate!
Don't let the carrier through!

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.490
- Where's the command car?
- Over there!

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.870
Ota, let's go!

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.700
Contact Captain Goto!

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:48.580
Asuma!

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:49.870
What?

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.000
The keys are
back in my room!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.250
What?

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.720
Excuse me, but I can't seem
to find the East Building.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.840
There's no time for that!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.770
Hey, where's my Patlabor?

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.140
YOUR Patlabor?

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.690
How can this be?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.060
How should I know?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.440
If it bothers you,
bring it back yourself!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:20.700
I will!

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.200
Halt!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.000
You won't get away!

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:34.250
The carrier has shut off
its radio! It's getting away!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.010
How lucky!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.430
I'm commandeering this!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.520
Uh... sure.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.980
Halt!

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:04.700
Alphonse

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.700
Asuka

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:16.130
Load those carriers!
Check the batteries!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.840
This is a first.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:25.220
They found two guards
tied up in the bathroom.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:29.720
Nowadays, you can't even
go to the bathroom in peace.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.480
Never mind. Aren't you joining
the emergency mobilization?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.310
No, they have a reckless streak.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:43.150
They always use force.
Even if we block all the streets,

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.110
they'd do more harm than good.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:45.740
But...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:50.700
Shinobu, please. I don't know
if we can make it in time...

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.960
As soon as Division 1
is ready, pull out!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.170
Uh...

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.010
What should we do, Sir?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.760
You can mind the store.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.550
Mind the store?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:11.930
You could take my patrol
car, but it's pretty small.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:20.820
Come in, Shinohara.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.980
Captain, where are you?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.650
Just pulling out.
What's the status?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.950
The target is on Koshu highway
heading for Takao, but...

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:30.830
What?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.870
There's a female officer
in pursuit of the target.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:35.580
A female officer?

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:39.630
Yeah, a strange girl.
She kept saying she was late.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.550
She was here for the
Labor aptitude test.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.420
Well, help her out
if you can.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.470
Help her out?

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.690
Hold on!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.340
Act like an officer!

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:26.670
Sorry, I'll explain later.
I need to borrow this!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.780
Now behave yourself!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.290
Attention criminals:

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:11.260
Give me back my Patlabor!

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.650
I won't let you
get away!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:35.780
I did it!

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.590
So the woman's gone?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:46.630
Yes.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:52.970
I'm sure she's okay. You
shouldn't assume the worst.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:54.720
But, Captain...

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.510
Don't worry about her.
She'll be fine.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.180
Do you know her,
Captain?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.190
Where's the target now?

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.440
Jimba highway,
heading west.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.990
Hmmm, no turnoffs.
There's no need for heroics.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.120
Just follow
them and observe.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:15.820
Roger!

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:21.450
We'll never catch
them on the ground.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.830
I'm going to approach from the
sky. Take the car back for me.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:34.090
Ah... that
new car smell!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.200
Alphonse.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.370
If they already outgun us...

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.790
what's the point
in following them?

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:09.040
I guess there's
no point.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.170
None?

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.380
It's better than just
listening to you talk.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.300
Show some respect for
your senior officers!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.760
I'll save you!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.430
And stop using
that funny voice!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.510
It wasn't me!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.850
You're set up the same way
you were in the simulator.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.480
- Do you read me?
- Who's there?

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.270
Special Vehicles, Second Section,
Division 2: Asuma Shinohara.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:34.360
Good. I'm transmitting
from inside the Ingram.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.950
Can you pilot it?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.030
I don't know all the options,
but in general, yes.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:43.410
Don't lie! That's the first
step toward a life of crime!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.830
You're too obnoxious.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:51.290
Listen. There's an emergency
deck-up switch under your seat.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:06.100
When the carrier stops,
move the deck up...

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:09.650
then escape in the confusion.
When the carrier stops...

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:11.940
Oh, we've stopped!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:14.940
Good work.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:18.240
I did my part.
From here on, it's all yours.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.370
We'll disassemble it,
and no one will ever know.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.500
Is someone inside?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.580
Of course not!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.680
It's moving!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.790
This is what
I've dreamed of!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.000
Stop dreaming and
look around you!

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:13.710
Oh, no!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.420
What should I do?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.090
You're equipped with a
37 mm revolver-cannon.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.180
Really? What
great equipment!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.640
It isn't loaded, but
it may scare them.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.860
Halt or I'll shoot!

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.650
She's bluffing.
The gun isn't loaded.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:39.030
They figured it out.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.240
Well, do your best!

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.820
Do my best? HOW
should I do my best?

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.570
Set your suspension
to C-Mode.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.450
The auto-balancer
will handle the legs.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.660
Trust the Ingram's
design and fight.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:55.840
Be serious! If I fought, my
Patlabor might get hurt!

00:19:56.090 --> 00:20:01.170
Your choice. If you stand there,
they'll turn you into scrap.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.430
I won't let that happen!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.730
Wow! I want a
piece of this action!

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:16.900
Idiot, you'll be crushed!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.190
Take that!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.450
Something came
out of his arm!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.160
It's an electromagnetic
baton. Use it.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.100
On your right!

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.900
She's good!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:06.070
Halt! This is Special Vehicles,
Second Section, Division 2.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.700
Freeze!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:40.230
Goto here...
everything's under control.

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:42.280
Sorry to send you
out for nothing.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.780
All units,
return to base.

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.920
They stole this just to study it...

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.930
to avoid spending money on
research and development.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:13.140
Some people just can't
handle fair competition.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:14.810
Hey, everybody...

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:19.230
while we're all here
to see the new Labor...

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.020
let me introduce our
newest team member.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:28.400
Special Vehicles, Second
Section, Division 2...

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:30.570
Noa Izumi,
reporting for duty!

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:19.220
Some woman named Clancy Kanuka
suddenly shows up...

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:21.640
on the last day
of our Ingram training...

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:24.060
Looking to get in
on the big tournament.

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:25.690
Why is SHE here?

00:24:25.770 --> 00:24:27.190
No way! Really?

00:24:27.230 --> 00:24:29.730
Is she trying to become
the Ingram pilot?

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:31.530
But I want that job!

00:24:31.610 --> 00:24:33.450
Well, you'll just have to win.

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:35.320
Next episode: "Kanuka Appears!"

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:37.450
Target, Lock On!

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:41.450
Next episode

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:41.450
Kanuka Appears!
